sec.p:
The DPPH assay was performed following the procedure reported by Zengin & Aktumsek with slight modifications (Zengin and Aktumsek 2014). The extracts were solubilized in MeOH:H2O 80:20, sonicated and filtered (0.45 μm). 0.2 mL of each sample was added to 2 mL of 0.1 mM DPPH solution in methanol. After an incubation at room temperature in the dark for 30 min, the absorbance was read at 517 nm. A calibration curve of Trolox (y = 207.91x − 1.8704, R
2 = 0.9966) was prepared in a range of concentrations of 0.1–0.4 mM plotting the % I (percentage of inhibition) against Trolox concentration. The % I was calculated as follows: 1.8704;
%I=AbsControl−AbsSampleAbsControl×100
